{{smaller block|I got back on the 5th with the ''advance'', the remainder following as rapidly as the steamers could carry them.
{{right|''U. S. Grant'', Pers. Mem., I. 290.}}}}
'''8.''' In ''schools'', a lesson not previously learned: opposed to ''review''.—'''9.''' Advancement; promotion; preferment: as, an ''advance'' in rank or office.—'''10.''' An offer or tender.
{{smaller block|The ''advance'' of kindness which I made was feigned.
{{right|''Dryden'', All for Love, iv.}}}}
'''11.''' In ''com.'': (''a'') Addition to price; rise in price: as, an ''advance'' on the prime cost of goods; there is an ''advance'' on cottons. (''b'') A giving beforehand; a furnishing of something before an equivalent is received, as money or goods, toward a capital or stock, or on loan, or in expectation of being reimbursed in some way: as, A made large ''advances'' to B.
{{smaller block|I shall, with great pleasure, make the necessary ''advances''.
{{right|''Jay''.}}
The account was made up with intent to show what ''advances'' had been made.
{{right|''Kent''.}}}}

